We are just five sleeps away from Apple's unveiling of its new-generation iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max models, not forgetting its first foldable iPhone.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iPhone-18-Pro-What-We-Know-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1062356" /><br/>
Apple is expected to introduce the devices at its annual iPhone fall event, which is this year carrying the tagline "<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/26/apple-iphone-event-2026/">Surprise and shine</a>." The event takes place on Wednesday, September 9. To help you get some shuteye in the meantime, here's a rundown of the features we're expecting from Apple's iPhone 18 Pro models.<br/>
<ul><br/>
<li><strong>Overall Design:</strong> The iPhone 18 Pro models are expected to stick to the overall iPhone 17 Pro design, but they could feature a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/11/11/iphone-18-pro-drop-rear-two-tone-look/">more seamless rear casing</a> with less contrast between the glass and aluminum frame.</li><br/>
<li><strong>Battery Life:</strong> The iPhone 18 Pro Max is rumored to feature a larger <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/02/06/iphone-18-pro-max-next-level-battery-life/">5,100–5,200 mAh battery</a> and a slightly thicker, heavier design as a result.</li><br/>
<li><strong>Smaller Dynamic Island:</strong> Apple is expected to <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/09/13/iphone-18-smaller-dynamic-island-rumor/">shrink the Dynamic Island</a>, made possible by moving some Face ID components beneath the display.</li><br/>
<li><strong>Upgraded Display:</strong> The iPhone 18 Pro models are said to use a more <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/05/06/iphone-18-pro-ltpo-display-upgrade-samsung/">power-efficient LTPO+ display</a>, supplied by Samsung Display and LG Display.</li><br/>
<li><strong>A20 Pro Chip:</strong> Apple's next-generation chip will use TSMC's advanced 2nm process, including <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/08/12/kuo-on-iphone-18-a20-chip-packaging/">Wafer-Level Multi-Chip Module (WMCM) technology</a>, which should bring improvements to performance and power efficiency.</li><br/>
<li><strong>C2 Modem:</strong> Apple's next-generation in-house cellular modem <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/03/17/iphone-18-pro-c2-modem-rumor/">could feature</a> in the Pro models, offering faster speeds, and improved efficiency. However, it's possible the C2 still lacks mmWave capability, and that the devices will use a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/02/iphone-18-pro-could-use-qualcomm-modem-in-the-us/">Qualcomm modem</a> in the United States and Apple's C2 modem in other parts of the world.</li><br/>
<li><strong>New Camera Sensor:</strong> Samsung is believed to have developed a new <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/01/10/iphone-18-samsung-camera-sensor-report/">three-layer stacked image sensor</a> for the iPhone 18 Pro lineup that improves responsiveness, noise, and dynamic range.</li><br/>
<li><strong>Variable Aperture:</strong> The 48-megapixel Fusion camera on both iPhone 18 Pro models is expected to gain a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/10/27/iphone-18-pro-variable-aperture-camera/">variable aperture</a> for greater control over light and depth of field.</li><br/>
<li><strong>5G Satellite Internet:</strong> The iPhone 18 Pro models could support full <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/10/24/iphone-18-pro-full-5g-satellite-internet-rumor/">5G connectivity via satellite</a>, which would be quite an expansion of Apple's existing satellite-based emergency features.</li><br/>
<li><strong>Simplified Camera Control:</strong> Apple is said to have <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/10/28/iphone-18-camera-control-capacitive/">redesigned the Camera Control button</a> to use pressure sensing without a separate capacitive layer, simply to reduce complexity and cost.</li><br/>
<li><strong>New Colors:</strong> Apple has reportedly tested several new finishes, but we're betting on these three: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/02/leaked-iphone-18-pro-parts-point-to-three-colors/">Light Blue, Dark Cherry, and Silver</a>. We no longer expect a Black option.</li><br/>
<li><strong>iOS 27:</strong> The iPhone 18 Pro will ship with <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a> and its overhauled Siri AI experience, which includes onscreen awareness, personal context, web knowledge, and expanded Apple Intelligence features.</li><br/>
</ul>Apple has held its fall event in the first two weeks of September in each of the last several years, with new iPhones typically going on sale the following Friday. It has been <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/28/iphone-18-pro-pre-orders-may-start-at-unusual-time/">rumored</a> that iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max pre-orders will begin on Saturday, September 12 at 12 a.m. Pacific Time this year.<br/>
